# Fimmick AEO — environment variables
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Every entry below says what BREAKS when it is
# missing, not just what it is — several failures are silent, or look like an
# unrelated outage. There is no startup validation: db() and auth() are lazy
# singletons specifically so the build survives missing config, so a missing
# variable surfaces at first use rather than at boot.

# ─── Required in production ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Neon connection string. Without it every DB path 500s; /api/scan returns an
# explicit "missing DATABASE_URL" 500.
# Careful: the Neon driver echoes the full URL, password included, in its error
# messages. Never paste it into a shell command — pipe through
# `2>&1 | grep -v "postgresql://"` when scripting against it.
DATABASE_URL=

# ─── Which database is DATABASE_URL actually pointing at? ────────────────────
#
# lib/db.ts proves the answer against the connection itself before the first
# query: Neon exposes neon.project_id / neon.branch_id as GUCs, so the session
# that will run the queries says who it is in band, rather than being inferred
# from the variable that may itself be wrong. A mismatch throws; there is no
# opt-out flag.
#
# Why this is a RUNTIME check and not a test: on 2026-09-05 DATABASE_URL was
# found pointing at the AISO project as `neondb_owner` — the owner role, whose
# DDL rights migration 037 exists to take away — and had been for three days.
# Nothing caught it. A CI test would not have either: CI verifies CI's own
# binding, which was never the one that was wrong.
#
# None of these seven values is a secret. They are identifiers, safe in a log,
# a ticket, or a screenshot.

# REQUIRED. The binding guard throws if unset, so the app will not serve — the
# first query of every process fails with a message naming this variable.
# Deliberate: an application that cannot prove which database it is talking to
# should not serve. AISO is weathered-wave-50814522.
EXPECTED_NEON_PROJECT_ID=

# Optional; checked only when set. Leave UNSET for integration runs, whose
# branch id differs on every run — the harness sets the project id and clears
# this one for exactly that reason. Pin it in production if you want the
# guard to reject a preview branch as well as a wrong project.
EXPECTED_NEON_BRANCH_ID=

# Optional; checked when set. Should be aeo_app — pinning it is what turns the
# 2026-09-05 incident (right project, owner role) into a startup failure rather
# than three silent days.
EXPECTED_DB_ROLE=

# Optional; checked when set. Should be neondb.
EXPECTED_DB_NAME=

# Comma-separated blocklists. Always enforced when non-empty, and they beat the
# allow-list above: a connection matching both is a configuration error, and the
# safe reading of a contradiction is the forbidding one. Use them to name a
# project, branch or endpoint this deployment must never reach — the legacy
# red-firefly project, say, or the production branch from a staging deploy.
FORBIDDEN_NEON_PROJECT_IDS=
FORBIDDEN_NEON_BRANCH_IDS=
FORBIDDEN_DB_HOSTS=

# The OWNER connection string, used only by `npm run migrate`.
# DATABASE_URL above is the least-privilege application role (aeo_app, migration
# 037), which deliberately cannot run DDL. The runner does NOT fall back to
# DATABASE_URL -- unset, `npm run migrate` fails immediately and says so.
MIGRATE_DATABASE_URL=

# Neon Auth. BASE_URL is runtime-only; COOKIE_SECRET is required at BUILD time
# and must be >= 32 chars — `next build` fails collecting page data for
# /api/auth/[...path] without it, because that route calls auth().handler() at
# module scope. Vercel deploys fail, not just requests.
NEON_AUTH_BASE_URL=
NEON_AUTH_COOKIE_SECRET=

# HMAC key for the durable public-scan and funnel-event rate limiters. >= 32
# chars. The local-development fallback is deliberately withheld in production,
# so if this is unset there, EVERY anonymous scan and every scan-claim-intent
# returns 503 — the whole public funnel goes dark while authenticated smoke
# tests stay green. The most dangerous omission in this file.
PUBLIC_SCAN_RATE_LIMIT_SECRET=

# Signs public report share links AND the scan-claim intent cookie — two
# consumers, not one. >= 32 chars. Unset: share links 404, publish/rotate 503,
# and the scan-to-signup claim funnel degrades to a fixed 403.
REPORT_SHARE_SECRET=

# Stripe. Without the webhook secret, constructEvent throws and EVERY webhook
# returns 400 "Invalid signature" — subscriptions silently never provision.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Platform-provided on Vercel, but a hard dependency: production rate limiting
# throws unless VERCEL=1, so a self-hosted production deploy cannot serve
# anonymous scans at all.
# VERCEL=1

# ─── Required if the feature is enabled ──────────────────────────────────────

# Stripe price ids. Checkout guards these and returns a clean 500 per plan; the
# webhook does NOT — with them unset no price matches and tier resolution falls
# through, so a paid upgrade can resolve to the wrong plan.
STRIPE_PRICE_BASIC=
STRIPE_PRICE_PRO=
STRIPE_PRICE_ENTERPRISE=

# OpenRouter. Fix packs and AI report summaries throw without it. GEO checks
# c18/c19 degrade quietly to check_error instead, costing the caller points
# with no error surfaced anywhere.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Shared secret for the scheduled cron routes. At least 16 characters, or the
# routes return 500 rather than running.
#
# Scheduling comes from cloudflare/cron-worker/ (its wrangler.jsonc), NOT
# Vercel Cron — vercel.json no longer has a `crons` array (removed 2026-08-22).
# The worker sends `Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET` on three schedules:
# GET /api/cron/pulse (17 4 * * 1), GET /api/cron/evaluate-alerts (47 7 * * 1,
# deliberately after pulse because alerts read the rollup pulse writes), and
# GET /api/cron/trial-emails (0 9 * * *). All three routes are live — none is a
# 503 stub. The pulse driver then calls POST /api/pulse/run with an
# `x-cron-secret` header — two header shapes, one secret; evaluate-alerts
# accepts both shapes on its own handlers.
#
# Until the worker is deployed (docs/runbooks/deploy-cron-worker.md), nothing
# schedules these routes at all.
# (n8n has its own $env.CRON_SECRET; unrelated to this one.)
CRON_SECRET=

# Resend API key. Consumed by lib/resend.ts for BOTH alert-evaluation emails
# (sendAlertEmail, driven weekly by /api/cron/evaluate-alerts) and trial drip
# emails (sendTrialEmail, driven daily by /api/cron/trial-emails). Unset, every
# send throws and those emails silently never arrive.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Bearer token for the n8n MCP server in .mcp.json. Tooling only, not the app.
N8N_MCP_TOKEN=

# ─── Optional — fallbacks shown ──────────────────────────────────────────────

# Public origin for SEO canonicals, Stripe redirects and report share links.
# Falls back to https://aeo.fimmick.com (lib/app-origin.ts).
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=

# Fire-and-forget scan webhook. Unset = feature simply off, no user impact.
N8N_SCAN_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Falls back to alerts@fimmick-aeo.com.
RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=

# Trial drip email from-address. Falls back to hello@fimmick-aeo.com, and is
# independent of RESEND_FROM_EMAIL.
RESEND_TRIAL_FROM_EMAIL=

# Falls back to "FimmickAISO/1.0 (https://fimmick.com)".
WIKIPEDIA_USER_AGENT=

# ─── Currently dead — listed so nobody re-adds them expecting an effect ──────

# NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY — read by no source file; checkout is
#                  server-side only. (The @stripe/stripe-js package is likewise
#                  installed but never imported; removing the dependency is
#                  deferred to the UI-foundation phase.)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL / _ANON_KEY / SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY — the Neon
#                  migration is complete; no application code reads these.

# ─── Tests and E2E only ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# TEST_DATABASE_URL is set by the integration harness per run; do not set it by
# hand. NEON_API_KEY authenticates neonctl in CI instead of `neonctl auth`.
#
# REQUIRE_INTEGRATION_TESTS=1 makes `npm test` FAIL rather than skip when
# neonctl is unavailable — the command that proves the full suite ran.
# SKIP_INTEGRATION_TESTS=1 forces the skip deliberately.
#
# Playwright: BASE_URL, START_DEV_SERVER=1, CI, PLAYWRIGHT_TEST_EMAIL,
# PLAYWRIGHT_TEST_PASSWORD, PLAYWRIGHT_AUTH_STORAGE_STATE,
# PLAYWRIGHT_CLIENT_REPORT_FIXTURE, LIVE_SCAN_TARGET, SKIP_E2E_SEED.
